# ============================================================
# Production Environment — React Frontend
# ============================================================
# Copy to .env.production and set the real values before building.
#
#   cp .env.production.example .env.production
#   npm run build
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed with VITE_ to the browser, and it inlines
# them into the bundle at BUILD time, not at run time. Two consequences:
#
#   1. Anything here ends up readable in the shipped JavaScript. Never put a
#      secret, API key or database credential in this file — the backend's .env
#      is where those belong.
#   2. Changing a value means rebuilding. Restarting the container is not enough.
#
# When building the Docker image, pass the value as a build argument instead:
#   docker build --build-arg VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.example.edu/api .
# docker-compose.yml already wires this through for you.
# ============================================================

# Base URL of the Spring Boot API, including the /api context path and no
# trailing slash. In development this defaults to http://localhost:8080/api.
#
# Same-origin deployment (frontend and API behind one domain, which is what the
# bundled nginx config expects) — use a relative path so the browser calls the
# host it loaded the page from:
VITE_API_BASE_URL=/api

# Separate API domain instead? Use the absolute URL, and add this origin to
# APP_CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS in the backend environment or the browser will block
# the requests:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://api.placement.example.edu/api
